-- A module whose one error is a value cycle reports that cycle and nothing
-- else (checker-v2.md §13.1). `r` is
-- defined in terms of itself through a record field, which is
-- `cyclic_value`; and the `r` inside it could be given an evidence argument
-- (the `==`'s `strict_eq`) that `r`, which has no requirements, does not take.
-- The evidence-count assert must not run BEFORE `Cycles`, see a module with
-- no error yet, and add an INTERNAL ERROR at that `r` to the cycle
-- message. It runs last, gated on every error the module
-- reported, so the golden holds the cycle alone.
--
r =
    { f = \x -> if x == 0 then 0 else r.f (x - 1) }
